{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:21-8","provision":"BCO 21-8","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"21-8","title":"Section 21-8","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/21-8/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/21-8","current_text":{"html":"<p>After the installation, the heads of families of the congregation then present, or at least the ruling elders and deacons, should come forward to their pastor, and give him their right hand, in token of cordial reception and affectionate regard. <b>Questions for Installation</b>4 <i>4For assistant minister, substitute the word ‘serve' for ‘take charge of', and add the word ‘assistant' before ‘pastor'.</i></p>","text":"After the installation, the heads of families of the congregation then present, or at least the ruling elders and deacons, should come forward to their pastor, and give him their right hand, in token of cordial reception and affectionate regard. Questions for Installation4 4For assistant minister, substitute the word ‘serve' for ‘take charge of', and add the word ‘assistant' before ‘pastor'."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"14d73f7e5caf1d22e0514870dd30fcc69f8165cc","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"38e35af46c8cbdb12a9a00c82d72f7192575b5ec27348534148f2a834551edc4","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudication